CORE
ref_port2.sv

^\[main\.p0\] always main\.some_var == 1: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A ref port and its actual denote the same variable (1800-2017 23.2.2.3).
Module M increments some_ref every clock, so main.some_var is driven
through the ref port and must not hold its value; it then follows the
increment, and the property some_var == 1 is correctly REFUTED. Before
the fix, main.some_var kept its hold-its-value transition, which
contradicted the ref-port equality and made the transition system
unsatisfiable, so the property was vacuously PROVED (EXIT=0).
